.TH GIT-PROJECT 1 "2026-11-19" "git-project" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-project \- Automate bare repositories, isolated agent worktrees, and Beads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fIgit project\fR clone [--no-worktree | --worktree-name <name>] [--no-beads] <remote-url> <project-name>
\fIgit project\fR init [--no-worktree | --worktree-name <name>] [--no-beads] <project-name>
\fIgit project\fR init --all
\fIgit project\fR delete [-f | --force] <project-name>
\fIgit project\fR migrate [--dry-run] [--project-name <name>] [--keep-backup] [--fsck] <path>...
\fIgit project\fR migrate --all [--yes] [--keep-backup] [--fsck]
\fIgit project\fR worktree add [--fetch] <project-name> <wt-name> [start-point]
\fIgit project\fR worktree (remove | rm) [-f | --force] <project-name> <wt-name>
\fIgit project\fR worktree (list | ls) <project-name>
\fIgit project\fR get-reponame
\fIgit project\fR help
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-project\fR manages Git projects using bare repositories for shared Git
history, linked worktrees for isolated checkouts, and a shared Beads workspace
inside the bare repository for issue tracking across all worktrees of a project.
.PP
Each managed project stores:
.IP \(bu 2
its bare Git repository at \fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git\fR,
.IP \(bu 2
its shared Beads workspace at \fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git/.beads\fR
(automatically discovered by \fBbd\fR(1) from any linked worktree via Git's
common directory), and
.IP \(bu 2
its worktrees under \fI<worktreesRoot>/<wt-name>\fR.
.PP
Running \fBgit project --help\fR displays this manual page via Git's help
dispatch, while \fBgit project help\fR prints the built-in usage summary.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBclone\fR [--no-worktree | --worktree-name <name>] [--no-beads] <remote-url> <project-name>
Clone \fI<remote-url>\fR as a bare repository at \fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git\fR,
configure \fBremote.origin.fetch\fR to fetch all remote branches, create an
initial worktree at \fI<worktreesRoot>/<project-name>\fR (unless \fB--no-worktree\fR
or \fB--worktree-name\fR is given), and initialize a shared Beads workspace at
\fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git/.beads\fR with issue prefix
\fI<project-name>\fR unless \fB--no-beads\fR is specified.
.TP
\fBinit\fR [--no-worktree | --worktree-name <name>] [--no-beads] <project-name>
.TQ
\fBinit\fR --all
Initialize a new bare repository (default branch \fBmain\fR) at
\fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git\fR, create an initial worktree (unless
\fB--no-worktree\fR is given), and initialize a shared Beads workspace at
\fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git/.beads\fR with issue prefix
\fI<project-name>\fR unless \fB--no-beads\fR is specified.
If \fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git\fR already exists, \fBinit\fR is idempotent
and initializes the project's \fB.beads\fR database if it does not exist yet.
With \fB--all\fR, reinitializes every bare repository in \fI<reposRoot>\fR,
creating any missing \fB.beads\fR databases.
.TP
\fBdelete\fR [-f | --force] <project-name>
Delete the bare repository \fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git\fR (including its
colocated \fB.beads\fR directory). Refuses to delete if active linked worktrees
exist unless \fB-f\fR or \fB--force\fR is given, in which case every active
worktree is removed first.
.TP
\fBmigrate\fR [--dry-run] [--project-name <name>] [--keep-backup] [--fsck] <path>...
.TQ
\fBmigrate\fR --all [--yes] [--keep-backup] [--fsck]
Convert existing standard clones into the bare-repository and linked-worktree
layout by moving the \fB.git\fR directory while preserving uncommitted changes,
untracked and ignored files, stashes, local branches, and reflogs.
With \fB--all\fR, scans \fI<worktreesRoot>\fR and prints a dry-run plan unless
\fB--yes\fR is supplied.
.TP
\fBworktree add\fR [--fetch] <project-name> <wt-name> [start-point]
Create a linked worktree at \fI<worktreesRoot>/<wt-name>\fR from
\fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git\fR. With \fB--fetch\fR, runs
\fBgit fetch --prune origin\fR first. If \fI[start-point]\fR is provided, creates
branch \fI<wt-name>\fR at that start point; otherwise attaches an existing local
branch, tracks \fBorigin/<wt-name>\fR, or creates a new branch \fI<wt-name>\fR.
.TP
\fBworktree remove\fR [-f | --force] <project-name> <wt-name>
.TQ
\fBworktree rm\fR [-f | --force] <project-name> <wt-name>
Remove the linked worktree \fI<worktreesRoot>/<wt-name>\fR. Pass \fB-f\fR or
\fB--force\fR to remove a worktree with uncommitted changes.
.TP
\fBworktree list\fR <project-name>
.TQ
\fBworktree ls\fR <project-name>
List worktrees registered with \fI<reposRoot>/<project-name>.git\fR.
.TP
\fBget-reponame\fR
Print the managed project name for the current Git worktree.
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Print the built-in usage summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--no-worktree\fR
For \fBclone\fR and \fBinit\fR, create only the bare repository without an
initial worktree. Mutually exclusive with \fB--worktree-name\fR.
.TP
\fB--worktree-name\fR <name>
For \fBclone\fR and \fBinit\fR, name the initial worktree \fI<name>\fR instead
of \fI<project-name>\fR. Mutually exclusive with \fB--no-worktree\fR.
.TP
\fB--no-beads\fR
For \fBclone\fR and \fBinit\fR, skip initializing a shared Beads workspace.
.TP
\fB-f\fR, \fB--force\fR
For \fBdelete\fR and \fBworktree remove\fR, force removal of active or dirty
worktrees.
.TP
\fB--fetch\fR
For \fBworktree add\fR, fetch and prune \fBorigin\fR before creating the worktree.
.TP
\fB--all\fR
For \fBmigrate\fR, inspect all directories under \fI<worktreesRoot>\fR. Dry-run by
default unless \fB--yes\fR is also passed.
.TP
\fB--dry-run\fR
For \fBmigrate\fR, print the migration plan without making changes.
.TP
\fB--yes\fR
For \fBmigrate --all\fR, execute the migration plan instead of performing a dry run.
.TP
\fB--project-name\fR <name>
For single-path \fBmigrate\fR, override the project name derived from
\fBremote.origin.url\fR.
.TP
\fB--keep-backup\fR
For \fBmigrate\fR, keep a backup copy of the original \fB.git\fR directory under
\fI<reposRoot>/.migrate-backup\fR.
.TP
\fB--fsck\fR
For \fBmigrate\fR, run \fBgit fsck --connectivity-only\fR after moving the
repository.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Locations are resolved in the following order of precedence:
.SS Environment variables
.TP
\fBGIT_PROJECT_REPOS_ROOT\fR
Path to the bare repositories directory.
.TP
\fBGIT_PROJECT_WORKTREES_ROOT\fR
Path to the worktrees directory.
.SS Git configuration
Keys in the \fB[project]\fR section:
.TP
\fBproject.reposRoot\fR
Path to the bare repositories directory.
.TP
\fBproject.worktreesRoot\fR
Path to the worktrees directory.
.SS Defaults
.TP
\fBreposRoot\fR
\fI~/projects/repos\fR
.TP
\fBworktreesRoot\fR
\fI~/projects/worktrees\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-worktree (1),
.BR bd (1)
